# ==== T-FMT-C · inline suite, MULTI-LINE child, header trailing comment
#
# THE ONE CELL IN THIS DIRECTORY THAT IS NOT A FIXPOINT — see the `.expected`
# companion. When an inline suite's single statement spans several lines and
# the header carries a trailing comment, the comment cannot stay on the header
# line: emitting it there puts the statement inside the comment and the file
# stops parsing.
#
# The comment is CLAIMED at the header (which is what stops the nested
# match-arm loop's leading hook from pulling it down into the arm list, where
# it would document the wrong thing) and INJECTED after the child's last line.
# It reparses, nothing is lost, and a second pass is a fixpoint — but the
# comment MOVES, and that is the pinned, chosen behaviour rather than an
# accident.

void main():
    int y = 2
    if true: int x = match y:
        case 2:
            20
        else:
            30    # note
    print(1)
